        "original_id": "891d9ba4-9d75-5473-b5db-0f39311e1cb0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Auty, Mary Plazas\n- Works: La Bohème (2009 film), \"Walking in the Air\", La bohème\n- Places: Ethiopia, Britain, continental Europe\n- Organizations: St Paul's Cathedral choir, Stiff Records\n- Roles: English operatic tenor, choirboy\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Robert Auty was born on 4 November 1969 and is an English operatic tenor.\n- Peter Auty has worked with most of the major opera companies in Britain and with a number of companies in continental Europe.\n- In the film featuring the song \"Walking in the Air,\" St Paul's Cathedral choirboy Peter Auty performed the song, and the recording was reissued in 1985 on Stiff Records and again in 1987.\n- The 2009 film La Bohème is four minutes long and features images of harsh life in Ethiopia.\n- The 2009 film La Bohème is set to the duet \"O soave fanciulla\" from Puccini's opera La bohème, sung by Peter Auty and Mary Plazas.",
